  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Trials for standardisation seafreight Kenya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">For the Kenya combi-track on agro logistics the transition to multi modal transport is key. This is including the transition of transport of flowers and vegetables by sea freight. However, this is still in an experimental phase in which best practices and standards are needed in order to move the sector ahead.By combining the development of technical standards with practical validation through real shipments, the project will increase confidence among stakeholders, including growers, exporters, logistics providers, and European buyers, identify and resolve operational issues related to product quality and supply chain logistics and support the adoption of sea freight as a sustainable, reliable, and competitive transportation solution.</narrative>
  </description>
